# LUCI Design — Minimalist & De-boxed

**Existing assets:** this rule still governs shipped newsletter, messaging docs, emails, and hub resources unless a redesign is requested.

**New assets:** follow `luci-modern-design-guidelines.mdc` (full system: tracks, spacing, type application, contrast, §8 checklist). Pick track by copy density. Brand colors, fonts, and voice stay here and in `luci-messaging-voice.mdc`. Flagship: Issue 01 newsletter.

LUCI is a modern, edgy 2026 tech brand. Let **whitespace, typography, and hairlines** carry structure — not stacked containers. Boxes are the exception, never the default.

## Do
- **Separate with space and hairlines.** Use a single 1px divider (`rgba(255,255,255,0.1)` on dark, `var(--rule-light)` on light) or generous padding instead of bordered boxes.
- **Keep corners sharp** (`border-radius: 0`) — a defining brand trait.
- **Reserve the 4px mint accent bar** for true callouts and pull quotes only (plus the masthead signature). Don't repeat it on every element.
- **Tabular data → de-boxed lists.** Render comparisons as a definition list / stacked rows with hairline separators, not an HTML `<table>` with cell borders (also avoids mobile horizontal scroll).
- **Callouts are the exception that *should* be contained.** Tips/asides = a contained block (4px mint left bar, sharp corners, padding) bracketed by whitespace — never a full-bleed section flush against another colored section, or they bleed together.
- **Newsletter section rhythm:** alternate `sec--white` / `sec--light` for articles; `sec--marquee` (sand + larger headline) for the lead field story; callouts on `sec--white`; reserve `sec--deep` for Closing/Footer — never a mid-issue article.
- **Minimum label size 10–11px.** Micro-labels use Space Grotesk semibold at ≥10px.
- **Contrast:** secondary text ≥ ~0.8 opacity on dark; never ship near-invisible text (e.g. 0.35).
- **Typography: heads in Space Grotesk, body copy in Inter.** Headlines, section titles, kickers, labels, and metric numerals use **Space Grotesk** (600–700 for headings) — the structure tier (Tier 2). **All running body copy / paragraph text / descriptions / decks / notes / attributions / table & list copy use Inter — always, in every asset** (documents, sales collateral, emails, web, hub). This is non-negotiable: copy text (non-head) is never Space Grotesk. See `luci-modern-design-guidelines.mdc` §3.1.
- **Syncopate — accent only, sparingly (Tier 1, display).** Reserve for high-attention moments where uppercase display type earns its legibility cost: primary CTA buttons, hero billboard words (e.g. single-word marquee), newsletter lead marquee. **Not** for document headers, capability decks, messaging guides, section chapters, or any paragraph-length headline.
- **Inter — the body/copy font, always.** Inter is the typeface for all non-head copy: running body, descriptions, decks, notes, attributions, table/list copy, and the diagram recede layer (node/data labels, captions, legends, annotations). Heads/labels/metric numerals stay Space Grotesk; display moments stay Syncopate. All three families are embedded (subset base64) in `assets/fonts/luci-brand-fonts.css` and in each canonical diagram SVG.

## Don't
- ❌ Don't wrap content in an outer `border: 1px` box and then add internal dividers too — pick one.
- ❌ Don't build 1px-gap grids that read like a spreadsheet (e.g. results/stat blocks).
- ❌ No drop shadows on flat content tiles; no gradients.
- ❌ Don't set body/copy text in Space Grotesk — **copy is always Inter**. Heads/labels/metric numerals stay Space Grotesk; display moments stay Syncopate. (Don't switch to Arial/Helvetica.)
- ❌ Don't use Syncopate for section headers or multi-line titles in documents, sales collateral, or hub resources — use Space Grotesk bold/semibold instead.

## Example
```css
/* ❌ BAD — boxed + gridlines */
.items { display: grid; gap: 1px; background: rgba(104,227,190,.12); border: 1px solid; }
.items li { background: var(--navy-mid); padding: 18px; }

/* ✅ GOOD — airy rows, hairline separators, sharp corners */
.items li { padding: 14px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1); }
```

See `LUCI Systems Design System/ui_kits/newsletter/the-signal-design-comparison.html` for the reference (Current vs Sharp de-boxed).
